{%- comment -%}
  snippets/portal-signin-invitation.liquid — what an anonymous visitor gets
  (spec task 19.2, design §5.7, §13.7).

  Requirements 1.5, 5.7, 13.7.

  ── WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, AND WHY EACH ABSENCE MATTERS ─────────────────
  Task 19.2: "no shell, no data hooks, no portal script for an anonymous visitor".
  Each of those is a specific hazard rather than tidiness:

    no `data-portal-section` root  the boot scan finds nothing, so no section can
                                   attempt a read for a customer who does not exist
    no portal script tag           an anonymous visitor downloads no portal
                                   JavaScript at all — the bundle cannot be the
                                   thing that discloses the portal's shape
    no live region, no nav         there is no account to navigate, and a rail of
                                   eight links to pages that will all refuse is a
                                   worse experience than one clear invitation
    no `athoor-portal.css`         nothing here needs it; the two rules used are
                                   inline-scoped below

  ── NO CREDENTIAL INPUT OF ANY KIND (Requirement 1.5) ─────────────────────────
  There is no `<form>`, no `<input>`, and no password field. This is a page a
  visitor can reach without signing in, and a login form on a merchant-authored
  page is a credential-harvesting shape a customer cannot distinguish from a real
  one. Authentication belongs to Shopify's own hosted flow, which is where these two
  links go and where the customer can see the URL they are typing into.

  ── IT DOES NOT REUSE `templates/page.account-landing.liquid` ─────────────────
  Task 19.2 says so explicitly, and the reason is visible in that file: it opens the
  theme's account DRAWER, which contains sign-in fields. Extending it would import
  exactly the credential surface the paragraph above rules out. The two links here
  are `routes.account_login_url` and `routes.account_register_url` and nothing else.

  Because the store uses Shopify's new customer accounts (D1 / OQ-1, Branch B),
  both routes resolve to Shopify's hosted authentication rather than to a theme
  template, so there is no theme login markup involved even indirectly.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="athoor-portal-invitation">
  <h1 class="athoor-portal-invitation__title">Your Athoor account</h1>
  <p class="athoor-portal-invitation__lead">
    Sign in to see your orders, your saved fragrances and the points you have earned.
  </p>
  <p class="athoor-portal-invitation__actions">
    <a class="athoor-portal-invitation__button" href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}">Sign in</a>
    <a class="athoor-portal-invitation__link" href="{{ routes.account_register_url }}">Create an account</a>
  </p>
</div>

